cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "truescore: statistics for LLM-judged evaluations"
message: "If you use truescore in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Punjwani
    given-names: Saif
repository-code: "https://github.com/SaifPunjwani/truescore"
url: "https://saifpunjwani.github.io/truescore/"
abstract: >-
  truescore corrects evaluation scores produced by an LLM judge for that judge's own error,
  using a small set of human labels. It implements prediction-powered inference, the
  Rogan-Gladen correction, confidence sequences valid under repeated inspection,
  HC3-robust judge-bias regression, per-segment correction with multiplicity control, and
  an exact permutation test for benchmark contamination. Interval coverage is verified by
  simulation rather than asserted.
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - llm-as-a-judge
  - prediction-powered inference
  - confidence sequences
  - statistics
license: Apache-2.0
